    "question": {
      ":question/id": "62034399-8e19-5dee-9f46-3c298fa0740c",
      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\n\n$$\n\\left(\\sin\\left(105^{\\circ}\\right)-\\cos\\left(105^{\\circ}\\right)\\right)^2\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Expand the square and use the Pythagorean identity.\n\nSet $x=105^{\\circ}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\sin x-\\cos x)^2 &= \\sin^2 x-2\\sin x\\cos x+\\cos^2 x \\\\ &=1-2\\sin x\\cos x \\\\ &=1-\\sin(2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sin x\\cos x &=\\sin(2x) \\\\ &=\\sin\\left(210^{\\circ}\\right) \\\\ &=- \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute this exact value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(\\sin\\left(105^{\\circ}\\right)-\\cos\\left(105^{\\circ}\\right)\\right)^2&=1-\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
